 "method_card": {
  "steps": [
   "Start with the intersection (overlap)",
   "Subtract intersection from each total to get the 'only' regions",
   "Don't forget the 'neither' region",
   "P(A|B) = n(A∩B) / n(B)",
   "P(A∪B) = P(A) + P(B) − P(A∩B)"
  ],
  "title": "Venn Diagrams & Conditional Probability",
  "content": "<p><strong>Venn diagrams</strong> show overlapping sets. \\(A \\cap B\\) = intersection (both). \\(A \\cup B\\) = union (either). Fill from the intersection outwards.</p><p><strong>Conditional probability:</strong> \\(P(A|B) = \\frac{P(A \\cap B)}{P(B)}\\) — probability of A given B has occurred.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>40 students: 25 play football, 18 play tennis, 10 play both. P(football | plays tennis)?</strong></p><p>P(F|T) = 10/18 = 5/9.</p>"
 },
